  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The correct order of relative basicity of amines in the gas phase is $3^{\\circ}>2^{\\circ}>1^{\\circ}>\\mathrm{NH}_3$ The alkyl group releases electron and thus, tends to disperse the positive charge of the alkyl ammonium ion and therefore stabilises it. Since, $\\mathrm{NH}_4{ }^{+}$(from $\\mathrm{NH}_3$ ) has no such alkyl group, it is not stabilised to such an extent as alkylammonium ion.",
    "image": null
